{
  "requirement": "Usage MUST record each provider request's outcome and available input/output\ntoken counts, including retries, with cached or reasoning-token counts when\nprovided, and for a failed request the failure under\n{cite}`requirements.authoring.usage_requests.failures`. Missing measurements MUST be recorded as unavailable, not zero.\nRun totals MUST include request and tool-call counts by tool, elapsed time, and\navailable token usage, identifying incomplete totals without double counting\nprovider counters that overlap.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.authoring.usage_requests`. I did not read implementation source. The checks below come from the supplied test text only.\n\n**Per-request outcome, including retries**\n- `throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt` sends 5 throttled attempts and then a success. It asserts `request_count == 6`, \"failed\" for each of the 5 retried attempts, and \"completed\" for the last.\n- `unanswered_requests_are_abandoned_and_retried` asserts \"failed\" followed by \"completed\" for a request that never got an answer.\n- `success_resets_backoff_and_retries_keep_history_without_repeating_tools` asserts 4 requests recorded across two retries.\n- `cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals` asserts the \"cancelled\" outcome.\n\n**Input and output token counts per request**\n- `token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown` and `partial_failure_retains_available_totals_and_optional_measurements` assert per-request input counts.\n- The CLI tests assert per-run totals against several provider shapes:\n  - Ollama (33 in / 21 out) in `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free`.\n  - Bedrock (38 / 10) in `bedrock_cli_uses_selected_profile_region_and_converse_tools`.\n  - OpenAI Responses (22 / 14) in `openai_responses_replays_tool_calls_and_records_usage`.\n\n**Cached and reasoning tokens when provided**\n- The unit test above asserts totals for cached (60), cache creation (20) and reasoning (10).\n- `openai_responses_replays_tool_calls_and_records_usage` asserts cached 6 and reasoning 4.\n- `claude_requests_carry_cache_checkpoints_and_record_cache_usage` asserts per-request and total cache reads and writes.\n\n**Missing measurements recorded as unavailable, not zero**\n- `partial_failure_retains_available_totals_and_optional_measurements` asserts that an unreported cached count gives a null total.\n- It asserts that a failed request's tokens are null.\n- It asserts that an explicit `cached_input_tokens(0)` gives 0, while an unreported reasoning count stays null.\n- `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text` asserts that tokens are null and `complete == false` when no request produced counts.\n\n**Run totals**\n- Request counts are asserted in several tests.\n- Tool-call counts by tool, plus failures and skips, are asserted in `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text`. Unknown tool names are bucketed as \"unknown\".\n- Elapsed time for both the run and each request is asserted in `completed_requests_and_the_run_record_elapsed_time` and in the cancelled-request test.\n- Available token usage is asserted as a sum over the requests that reported it.\n\n**Incomplete totals**\n- `complete` is asserted false in flight, after a failed request with no usage, after cancellation, and with mixed optional counters.\n- It is asserted true when every request was measured.\n\n**No double counting of overlapping counters**\n- With input 100 and cached 30 per request, the total input is 200 and cached is 60. Cached input is therefore not added into the input total.\n- The Bedrock responses carry `totalTokens` of 24. The asserted totals are input 38 and output 10, so the overlapping total counter is not summed in.\n\n**Failure recording under `requirements.authoring.usage_requests.failures`**\n- Per the task, that requirement's own tests are not reassessed here. The cited failure behavior is nonetheless exercised in the subject's case.\n- `throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt` and `failed_submission_can_be_confirmed_on_a_later_attempt` assert the exact failure object: `{http_status, error_code, retried}`.\n- `failed_submission_can_be_confirmed_on_a_later_attempt` also asserts `retried` flips from false to true.\n- The exact-equality assertions would catch any message text being added.\n\nI found no obligation of the requirement that lacks a test with a relevant assertion.",
  "references": "919fa8cdcc84f5770b5389c34bd3953c784f52cda01f7ce8314d9f1ed0606f2e",
